From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JarvisNano <jarvisnano@local>
Date: Thu, 22 May 2026 09:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] waveform: byte-swap colours to panel bus order (fix white render)

HARDWARE FEEDBACK (build 0030+0031): the reactive waveform rendered WHITE
instead of arc-reactor orange.

ROOT CAUSE: the CO5300 QSPI AMOLED runs with the emote engine's colour-swap
flag ON (emote.c emote_should_swap_color → true for non-dsi/rgb panels). The gfx
software blend has a fast path for fully-opaque pixels that copies the source
pixel to the framebuffer WITHOUT swapping (gfx_blend.c:190,
`last_res_color = src_buf[x]`). The working emote anim faces land correct
because the EAF decoder bakes the swap into the palette at decode time
(gfx_eaf_dec.c eaf_palette_get_color: swap=true → __builtin_bswap16). Our
runtime RGB565A8 buffer wrote UNswapped pixels, so on the swap-expecting panel
the bytes were misread → wrong colour.

FIX: one line — pre-swap the RGB565 colour constants to panel bus order in the
RGB565() macro, matching the anim path's convention. All COL_* constants inherit
it. Partial-alpha glow still works: gfx_blend_color_mix swaps src+dest into
native order, mixes, swaps the result back, which is consistent for a bus-order
dest buffer.

  -#define RGB565(r,g,b) ((uint16_t)(((r&0xF8)<<8)|((g&0xFC)<<3)|(b>>3)))
  +#define RGB565(r,g,b) ((uint16_t)__builtin_bswap16((uint16_t)(((r&0xF8)<<8)|((g&0xFC)<<3)|(b>>3))))

Verified the bswap: #FFE25E→bus 0x0BFF, #F5870B→bus 0x21F4, #6A3A05→bus 0xC069
(none are 0xFFFF white).

No new bootstrap apply step: the fix lives in the vendored
firmware/emote/waveform.c, and apply_reactive_waveform_face_patch now ALWAYS
re-copies that file (moved the cp above the idempotency guard) so source-of-truth
edits propagate on incremental trees too. Clean rebuilds already re-copy it.

SECOND FIX (same patch) — SPIRAL render: the user also saw a diagonal spiral,
the textbook signature of a row-stride/descriptor mismatch. Compared our
gfx_image_dsc_t to the working reference (test_apps assets/icon_rgbd565A8.c):
the reference sets ONLY cf/magic/w/h/data_size/data as ONE designated-initializer
literal, leaving stride+flags zero. Ours set header.stride=w*2 via field-by-field
assignment on the live packed-bitfield struct. The decoder ignores header.stride
(src_stride = header.w, gfx_img.c:117), but the field-by-field RMW on a packed
bitfield header (vs the reference's single packed write) is the suspected spiral
cause. Fix: build the dsc as one designated-initializer literal matching the
reference, stride/flags zero. data_size = w*h*2 + w*h = 167760 (same formula the
reference uses: 65*65*2 + 65*65 = 12675).

Both fixes ship together — one flash, distinct diagnostic outcomes:
  - orange + correct shape → both mattered, done.
  - orange + still spiral → colour was it, dsc theory wrong → 0034 pivots to
    object geometry / emote_create_obj_by_type image init.
  - still white + spiral → deeper cause (cross-core PSRAM cache coherency, or the
    create-by-type image object not wired like layout.json-defined objects).

The "not full screen / thin band" feedback is a SEPARATE shape redesign
(horizontal 466x120 strip → concentric rings + radial arcs at 466x466 for the
round panel) — deferred to patch 0034 after the user confirms orange + no spiral.
---
diff --git a/components/common/emote/waveform.c b/components/common/emote/waveform.c
--- a/components/common/emote/waveform.c
+++ b/components/common/emote/waveform.c
@@ define RGB565 @@
-#define RGB565(r, g, b)   ((uint16_t)(((r & 0xF8) << 8) | ((g & 0xFC) << 3) | (b >> 3)))
+#define RGB565(r, g, b)   ((uint16_t)__builtin_bswap16((uint16_t)(((r & 0xF8) << 8) | ((g & 0xFC) << 3) | (b >> 3))))
@@ face_init_dsc @@
-    s_face.dsc[i].header.magic  = 0x19;
-    s_face.dsc[i].header.cf     = GFX_COLOR_FORMAT_RGB565A8;
-    s_face.dsc[i].header.w      = FACE_W;
-    s_face.dsc[i].header.h      = FACE_H;
-    s_face.dsc[i].header.stride = FACE_W * 2;
-    s_face.dsc[i].data_size     = FRAME_BYTES;
-    s_face.dsc[i].data          = s_face.buf[i];
+    s_face.dsc[i] = (gfx_image_dsc_t){
+        .header = { .cf = GFX_COLOR_FORMAT_RGB565A8, .magic = 0x19, .w = FACE_W, .h = FACE_H },
+        .data_size = FRAME_BYTES, .data = s_face.buf[i],
+    };
